WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
(Iron Dome rumbling)

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.560
- In the tiny Pacific paradise of Guam,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.263
Operation Iron Island is under way.

00:00:07.263 --> 00:00:09.950
(machines rumbling)

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.030
As China ramps its military
capabilities in the region,

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.750
US forces are testing the Iron Dome,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.120
a defense system capable

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.990
of firing missiles that
intercept short-range threats,

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.400
like rockets, mortars,
drones and cruise missiles.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.750
It's not that big.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.730
- No, it's not.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.040
And you can tell how big
the interceptors would be

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.340
by little pods.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.173
- Right, right.

00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:32.450
Chief Foreign Officer Caroline
Surprenant specializes

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.550
in the army's missile defense systems.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.700
She says the Iron Dome
could provide a new layer

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.650
of defense as threats in the region grow.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.840
What are these interceptors
capable of doing?

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.690
- While the platform is fixed
for the missile firing unit,

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.520
you'll see that the interceptors are able

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.119
to maneuver towards the threat.

00:00:49.119 --> 00:00:50.010
(sirens ringing)
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.900
- [Shelby] It's the
same system Israel uses

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.760
to shoot down rockets from Gaza.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.450
And it has been 90% effective.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.070
Testing of the Iron Dome
here comes just months

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.900
after a top military leader warned

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.040
that Guam's defenses are inadequate

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.700
against threats from China.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.860
- Guam is a target today.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.010
It needs to be defended and it needs

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.890
to be prepared for the threats

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.240
that will come in the future.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.700
- [Shelby] So what exactly
is the army testing?

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.330
And would the Iron Dome be enough

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.200
to protect this US territory,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.330
which is playing an
increasingly important role

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.184
in America's strategy to counter China?

00:01:23.184 --> 00:01:24.640
(pensive music)

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.560
It's often said that
America's day begins in Guam,

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.240
a volcanic island just 36 miles long

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.920
and blessed with lush mountains,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.563
beautiful beaches, and stunning sunsets.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.590
West of the International Date Line,

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.630
Guam is roughly 1/3 the distance
to China and North Korea

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.910
as it is to the mainland United States.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.180
And the military bases
on Guam are the closest

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.810
on American soil to the places

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.780
where China has been
exerting military influence

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:52.210
in Taiwan and the South China Sea.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.610
- She was here two commanders ago.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.730
- As a result, military officials say

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.460
Guam's strategic importance is growing.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.080
What role would Guam play

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.470
in the event of a conflict?

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:06.190
- In the event of any military operations

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.421
for the United States
in the Pacific region,

00:02:08.421 --> 00:02:10.420
Guam plays a role.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.060
- Rear Admiral Benjamin Nicholson

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.240
oversees all US forces in Guam

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.110
and Joint Region Marianas,

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.540
part of what the Pentagon says
is America's priority theater

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.850
and a region in which
the military says China

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.200
is a top concern.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.740
What does it mean when
you hear the Secretary

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.830
of Defense say China is the
number one pacing threat?

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.300
- You always wanna pace against

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.640
whoever's the fastest runner,

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.990
whoever can go the longest, the farthest.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.260
That's where you set your pace.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.660
And in today's environment,

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.160
that really becomes China.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.440
They're doing the most build up,

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.570
they're doing it the quickest

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.120
with the most advanced weapons.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.830
- Admiral Nicholson and other
officials we spoke to said

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.240
that the Iron Dome's deployment

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.340
is fulfilling a Congressional requirement

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.480
and is not a direct response to China.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.320
But it comes as the Defense
Department released new details

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.260
about China's growing
nuclear capabilities.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.560
China has been expanding
its nuclear arsenal

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.650
much faster than previously thought

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.800
according to a recent Pentagon report.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:05.410
Beijing could have about
700 nuclear warheads

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.030
in the next six years,

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.370
and defense experts says some

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.800
of the weapons it's been testing

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.950
could potentially complicate US defenses.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.720
According to the report
released in early November,

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.750
China may have already
established a nuclear triad,

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:22.250
the ability to launch nukes
from the air, land and sea.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.600
Beijing is also developing new MIRVs,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.810
intercontinental
ballistic missiles capable

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.690
of delivering multiple warheads

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.140
to multiple targets.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.700
The term MIRV is an acronym

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:35.710
for Multiple Independently
Targetable Re-Entry Vehicles.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.210
And over the summer, China
surprised US officials

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.080
when it tested a hypersonic missile

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.060
that orbited the Earth before maneuvering

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.660
toward its target.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.560
While the US still has
roughly 11 times more missiles

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.300
than China according to the Federation

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.880
of American Scientists,

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.930
the build-up has alarmed
some military leaders.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.930
And while the Iron Dome
wouldn't be capable

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:55.970
of defending against some

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:59.170
of China's more sophisticated
missiles, it could be used

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.470
to counter the country's
growing fleet of bombers

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.340
that are able to launch cruise missiles

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.853
in the event of a conflict.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:08.100
Guam has been threatened before.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.830
In 2017, North Korea said it
would fire missiles at Guam.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.240
And in a video released
on social media last year,

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:15.460
China's air force hinted

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.563
that a US base on Guam could be a target.

00:04:18.563 --> 00:04:21.180
(dramatic music)

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.530
Walking around the naval
and air bases here,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.850
which The Wall Street
Journal was given access to,

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.650
it's not hard to see why an
adversary might take interest

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.410
in the major military facilities

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.890
and assets that would play a
key role in a confrontation.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.810
What do you say to locals here

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:38.690
who are concerned that
the more service members,

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.330
the more assets arrive on Guam,

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.830
the more Guam becomes a target?

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.790
- We actually had a lot more people here

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.280
during the height of the Cold War.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.120
I wouldn't necessarily would say

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.810
that it would make us more of a target

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.920
but certainly, we put enough assets here.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.550
It also makes it easier for us

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:58.763
to defend the area when we
have additional resources here.

00:04:58.763 --> 00:05:02.120
- Guam is already home to a
key missile defense system,

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.570
which we were invited to film,

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.280
along with the Iron Dome.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.470
Just a few hundred yards behind Iron Dome

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.680
is the THAAD launcher,

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.150
the Terminal High Altitude
Area Defense system,

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:12.500
and a big reason why Iron Dome

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.230
is here in Guam in the first place

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.350
is to see if these two
systems can work together.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.660
The testing aims to determine

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.280
whether data from both systems

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.150
can be transmitted back to Hawaii

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.573
in a way that allows them to
function alongside each other.

00:05:25.573 --> 00:05:26.690
THAAD is designed to detect

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.560
and intercept ballistic missiles,

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.570
like some of the nukes developed
by North Korea and China.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:34.130
But it's not designed to
intercept short-range threats,

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:35.210
like cruise missiles,

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.180
which fly on flat, direct paths

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.270
that are more difficult
for missile defense radars

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.103
to pick up.

00:05:40.103 --> 00:05:41.740
So systems like the Iron Dome

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.760
could potentially fill that gap.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.070
- We always like to operate layered.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.330
So we never want just
one layer of defense,

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.380
so multiple layers is something

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.120
that we're always looking to achieve.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.180
- So far, the military says the Iron Dome

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.620
has shown encouraging results

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.310
in terms of integrating with THAAD

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:58.920
and it has worked well in Guam's hot

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.650
and humid environment.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.170
Plus, the testing being done here

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.780
could help inform a new
defense system being developed

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.510
for the army by Dynetics

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.040
since the military doesn't plan

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.250
to buy additional Iron Domes.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.540
Did we have anything at this
lower level before Iron Dome?

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.910
- We have other air defense systems

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.280
but we don't have a lot
of them in our arsenal.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.240
So the more that we're
able to use and employ,

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.880
the more flexibility we have

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.960
with defense and planning.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.610
- [Shelby] The Iron Dome
is scheduled to return

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.200
to the mainland in December,

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.260
and the data from the
testing will be analyzed

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.580
as part of a bigger plan

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:38.386
to achieve a 360-degree defense of Guam.

00:06:38.386 --> 00:06:41.053
(pensive music)

